@token = 1000000000

### === Setup / lookups ===

### Get account info (active account)
GET http://localhost:4040/accounts/255700000001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get balance
GET http://localhost:4040/accounts/260970000000/balance
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get ledger (should be empty at first)
GET http://localhost:4040/accounts/260970000000/ledger
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### === Auth failure cases ===

### No auth header (should 401)
GET http://localhost:4040/accounts/260970000000

### Wrong token (should 401)
GET http://localhost:4040/accounts/260970000000
Authorization: Bearer wrong-token


### === PAYEE SIDE: reserve -> commit (money arriving for this customer) ===
### Reserve does NOT touch the balance — Bob never had this money yet.
### Only commit actually credits the account.

### Reserve funds (a pending marker only — balance is NOT touched)
POST http://localhost:4040/funds/reserve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "account_id": "260970000000",
  "amount": 100.0,
  "currency": "ZMW"
}

### Check balance - should be UNCHANGED (reserve never touches it)
GET http://localhost:4040/accounts/260970000000/balance
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Commit (replace reserve_id with the one from the reserve response above)
### This is the ONLY point the balance actually changes on the payee side.
POST http://localhost:4040/funds/commit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reserve_id": "REPLACE_ME"
}

### Check balance again - should be 100 HIGHER now, only after commit
GET http://localhost:4040/accounts/260970000000/balance
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Check the ledger - should show a PENDING entry (balance unchanged) then a CREDIT entry (balance up)
GET http://localhost:4040/accounts/260970000000/ledger
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### === PAYEE SIDE: reserve -> unreserve (hold gets cancelled, nothing ever really happened) ===

### Reserve funds again
POST http://localhost:4040/funds/reserve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "account_id": "260970000000",
  "amount": 50.0,
  "currency": "ZMW"
}

### Unreserve it (replace reserve_id) - balance should NOT change, since it was never touched
POST http://localhost:4040/funds/unreserve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reserve_id": "REPLACE_ME",
  "reason": "downstream transfer failed"
}

### Try to unreserve the SAME one again - should 422, already RELEASED
POST http://localhost:4040/funds/unreserve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reserve_id": "REPLACE_ME",
  "reason": "trying again"
}

### Try to unreserve something already COMMITTED (use a reserve_id from the commit test above) - should 422
POST http://localhost:4040/funds/unreserve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reserve_id": "REPLACE_WITH_ALREADY_COMMITTED_ID",
  "reason": "wrong endpoint on purpose"
}


### === SIMULATE: stands in for the DFSP's own customer-facing app ===
### Toggle test/live by setting MODE when you start the mock:
###   MODE=test uvicorn app.main:app --port 4040        (no connector needed)
###   MODE=live uvicorn app.main:app --port 4040         (real connector must be running)

### Ask for a quote (never touches money, either mode)
POST http://localhost:4040/simulate/send-money
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "payer_account_id": "260970000000",
  "payee_id": "16135551212",
  "amount": 150.00,
  "send_currency": "ZMW",
  "receive_currency": "MWK"
}

### Accept the quote - ALWAYS really debits, regardless of mode
### (replace transaction_id / home_transaction_id with the ones from the quote response above)
POST http://localhost:4040/simulate/accept-quote
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transaction_id": "TXN494BFD64EA584F18",
  "home_transaction_id": "HTX76ADE405279B",
  "payer_account_id": "260970000000",
  "amount": 150.00,
  "currency": "ZMW"
}

### Check the balance dropped by 150 - the debit was real even in test mode
GET http://localhost:4040/accounts/260970000000/balance
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Check the ledger shows the DEBIT entry from the simulated accept
GET http://localhost:4040/accounts/260970000000/ledger
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### === PAYER SIDE: refund (reverses a real debit made via /simulate/accept-quote) ===
### Note: there's no standalone debit endpoint to test here — the connector
### never calls one directly. Debits only happen through /simulate/accept-quote
### above, matching how a real app debits its own CBS before telling the
### connector to proceed. Run the SIMULATE section above first, then come back
### here using the home_transaction_id it generated.

### Refund a debit - looked up by home_transaction_id (replace with a real one from a simulate/accept-quote response)
POST http://localhost:4040/debits/refund
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "home_transaction_id": "HTX76ADE405279B",
  "reason": "transfer failed downstream after debit"
}

### Check balance - should be back up by the refunded amount
GET http://localhost:4040/accounts/260970000000/balance
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Try refunding the SAME home_transaction_id again - should 422, already REFUNDED
POST http://localhost:4040/debits/refund
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "home_transaction_id": "HTX76ADE405279B",
  "reason": "trying again"
}

### Final ledger check - should show the full story in order
GET http://localhost:4040/accounts/260970000000/ledger
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
